    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The research plan recommends HOLD, and the evidence supports this balanced stance. AMZN is at its 60-day peak (~$180.38) in a bullish technical alignment (price above rising 10 EMA, 50 SMA, and 200 SMA; RSI at 61.90), with strong cash generation ($84.9B operating cash flow, ~$35.1B FCF). However, the stock is pressing against the upper Bollinger Band at $181.51 after rejection at $181.70, the MACD line remains below the signal line (bearish crossover persisting two weeks), and critical fundamental data (income statement, revenue growth, margins, valuation) plus news/sentiment are unavailable in this historical window. With no bearish catalyst to justify selling and no confirmation of a fresh breakout to justify buying at the peak, maintaining current exposure is the disciplined call. Any incremental buying should be gated on a MACD histogram turn positive with the MACD line crossing above the signal line, or a decisive close above $181.70 on above-average volume; a break below the 50 SMA at ~$170.51 would warrant reassessment.\n\n**Entry Price**: 181.7\n\n**Stop Loss**: 170.51\n\n**Position Sizing**: Hold current weight; gate any incremental buying on technical confirmation triggers (MACD bullish crossover or decisive close above $181.70 on above-average volume).\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
